CHAPTER 2| Population Characteristics
The SMAM for males in the urban and rural sector was similar at 27 years, likewise for females at 23 years. Since
2000, SMAM for males has increased from 26 years to 27 years and from 22 years to 23 years for females. Both have
increased by 1 year in the last 11 years.
There were variations in the SMAM between provinces from 27 years in SHP to less than 24 years in Milne Bay, EHP
and Gulf provinces. SMAM was lowest among males (26 years) in Milne Bay, Western, and EHP , whereas for females
(21 years) in Milne Bay, Manus and Gulf provinces (see Summary Indicators).
Relationship Status
The relationship status of each member of the household to the head of the household is presented in Table 2.3.
According to the 2011 census, 18% of population were heads of household and 14% were spouses to the head.
More than 46% were own children whilst 3% were step or adopted children. A further 17% were other relatives to
the head of household.
