Roman Catholic remained the major Christian denomination in PNG, accounting for 26% of the population, followed
by Evangelical Lutheran (18%) and Seventh Day Adventist (13%) as shown in Figure 2.1.
Due to the possible missionary influences in the past, there were major concentrations of particular Christian
denominations in some provinces. Such were found in AROB (Roman Catholic, 68%), Morobe province (Evangelical
Lutheran, 67%) and Northern Province (Anglican, 61%). (See Summary Indicators).
