Non-citizens
According to the 2011 census, 56% of the non-citizen population aged 15 years and over were married with higher
proportion among the females (66%) than males (51%). More than a quarter of non-citizen males and females were
never married, respectively. The SMAM for males was higher than females with 25 years and 23 years, respectively.
(See Summary Indicators).
More than 62% of non-citizen males aged 15 to 64 years were heads of households while 45% of non-citizen
females of the same age group were spouses.
About 52% of non-citizen populations were Christians of which more than one third (34%) were Roman Catholics
and a further 14% were Evangelical Lutherans as shown in Figure 2.2. However, more than 37% of the non-citizen
population did not belong to any religion, while 3% belonged to non-Christian religions.

